  "answer": "No, not by recent standards. The Aussie dollar is strong against the yen compared with a year or more ago, though it has eased somewhat since spring.\n\n- **Latest (October 2026):** A$1 buys about ¥109.67 (RBA, 4pm AEST, last observation in the month).\n- **Recent peak (April 2026):** ¥114.28, so the Aussie is about 4% below its high.\n- **A year earlier (October 2025):** ¥100.84, so the Aussie is about 9% stronger now.\n- **January 2025:** ¥96.14, so the Aussie is about 14% stronger now.\n\nOver the past 21 months, the Aussie has mostly risen against the yen, from a low of ¥91.43 in April 2025 to the April 2026 high. Its recent dip from that peak is modest.",
